SUMMARY:JPJ Memorial Turkey Trot
LOCATION:Moncus Park\, 2913 Johnston Street\, Lafayette
DESCRIPTION:*This is an externally hosted event produced by JPJ Memorial.* 
 Join us for the 5th Annual JPJ Memorial 1-mile Turkey Trot! The event will
  be held at 9am on Thanksgiving morning at Moncus Park in memory of Jean P
 aul Judice. Jean Paul believed that his message of loving our world began 
 with family and friends\; but\, he hoped that by spreading a message of un
 conditional love among his closest relationships\, change would be rippled
  across the universe. He knew that every person mattered and he loved them
  unconditionally. This year we are raising funds for St. Joseph Diner. The
  diner has served meals to those experiencing hunger and food insecurity s
 ince 1983. This race is the perfect setting to come together to show grati
 tude with your community. Learn more and register here: JPJ MEMORIAL TURKE
 Y TROT\n\nhttps://moncuspark.org/calendar-events/jpj-memorial-turkey-trot-
 2026/
URL:https://moncuspark.org/calendar-events/jpj-memorial-turkey-trot-2026/
